---
import { Marked } from 'marked';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { RFC_FILE, href } from '../config';
import { rfcSections } from '../lib/markdown';
import { exampleCard, problem } from '../lib/rfc';

const md = new Marked({ gfm: true });
const problemHtml = md.parseInline(problem()) as string;
const sec = rfcSections();
const rfc = (n: string) => `${href('/rfc/')}#${sec.get(n)}`;
// The diagram's boxes: a serif title and subtitle lines, the same in both layouts.
const boxes = [
  { title: 'Producers', wide: ['mail · calendar ·', 'project tools ·', 'agents · scripts'], tall: ['mail · calendar · project tools ·', 'agents · scripts'] },
  { title: 'Personal head', wide: ['stores cards ·', 'builds the brief ·', 'records decisions'], tall: ['stores cards · builds the brief ·', 'records decisions'] },
  { title: 'Person', wide: ['reads · decides ·', 'orders'], tall: ['reads · decides · orders'] },
];
const label = 'Producers send cards to the personal head with PUT /cards/{id} and read changes back with GET /changes; the head sends the person a brief, and the person sends back decisions. Every connection starts at the producer.';
---
<Base title="Protocol" path="/" description="A small HTTP protocol for the decisions agents, scripts and tools need from one person: cards in, decisions out.">
  <h1>Personal Brief Card Protocol</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Agents and tools share one person's decision interface without sharing a workflow engine or giving up ownership of
    their own data: the head records what reached the person and what they decided, and each producer stays
    authoritative for its own domain.
  </p>

  <figure class="flow">
    <svg class="wide" viewBox="0 0 680 206" role="img" aria-label={label}>
      <defs>
        <marker id="head-w" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0.5 L7,4 L0,7.5" class="tip" /></marker>
      </defs>
      {boxes.map((b, i) => (
        <g transform={`translate(${i * 265 + 0.5}, 0.5)`}>
          <rect width="149" height="112" rx="6" class="box" />
          <text x="75" y="34" class="title">{b.title}</text>
          {b.wide.map((l, j) => <text x="75" y={58 + j * 17} class="sub">{l}</text>)}
        </g>
      ))}
      <line x1="156" y1="40" x2="259" y2="40" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#head-w)" />
      <text x="207" y="31" class="code">PUT /cards/&#123;id&#125;</text>
      <line x1="259" y1="76" x2="156" y2="76" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#head-w)" />
      <text x="207" y="94" class="code">GET /changes</text>
      <line x1="421" y1="40" x2="524" y2="40" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#head-w)" />
      <text x="472" y="31" class="code">brief</text>
      <line x1="524" y1="76" x2="421" y2="76" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#head-w)" />
      <text x="472" y="94" class="code">decision</text>
      <path d="M75,120 C75,160 340,160 340,120" class="arrow loop" marker-end="url(#head-w)" />
      <text x="207" y="182" class="note">every connection starts at the producer</text>
    </svg>
    <svg class="tall" viewBox="0 0 328 470" role="img" aria-label={label}>
      <defs>
        <marker id="head-t" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0.5 L7,4 L0,7.5" class="tip" /></marker>
      </defs>
      {boxes.map((b, i) => (
        <g transform={`translate(0.5, ${[0, 200, 370][i]! + 0.5})`}>
          <rect width="327" height="88" rx="6" class="box" />
          <text x="164" y="32" class="title">{b.title}</text>
          {b.tall.map((l, j) => <text x="164" y={56 + j * 17} class="sub">{l}</text>)}
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x="164" y="112" class="note">every connection starts at the producer</text>
      <line x1="134" y1="126" x2="134" y2="196" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#head-t)" />
      <text x="126" y="166" class="code end">PUT /cards/&#123;id&#125;</text>
      <line x1="194" y1="196" x2="194" y2="126" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#head-t)" />
      <text x="202" y="166" class="code start">GET /changes</text>
      <line x1="134" y1="294" x2="134" y2="366" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#head-t)" />
      <text x="126" y="335" class="code end">brief</text>
      <line x1="194" y1="366" x2="194" y2="294" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#head-t)" />
      <text x="202" y="335" class="code start">decision</text>
    </svg>
  </figure>

  <p class="lede">
    A protocol for the point where software has to stop and ask a person. A producer submits a <em>card</em> to the
    person's <em>head</em>; the person decides; the producer reads the decision and carries on.
  </p>

  <h2>The problem</h2>
  <blockquote><p set:html={problemHtml} /></blockquote>
  <p class="muted">From §1 of the RFC.</p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Someone whose agents, scripts and tools each need a decision from them: a mail agent with a reply to approve, a
    project tracker with a milestone at risk, a calendar with a clash. Each one sends a card to the same head, so the
    person has one place to decide and one record of what they decided. The protocol is strictly personal; team work
    stays in team tools.
  </p>

  <h2>A card</h2>
  <p>A card is a markdown file with a small YAML header, or the same fields as JSON on the wire. This is the example from §3:</p>
  <pre><code>{exampleCard()}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The producer mints the <code>id</code>, so sending the same card twice is harmless. Once the person decides, the card
    is locked; a change needs a new card that supersedes it.
  </p>

  <h2>Three operations</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Request</th><th>Who</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Submit</td><td><code>PUT /cards/&#123;id&#125;</code></td><td>A producer, with its token</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sync</td><td><code>GET /changes?after=&#123;seq&#125;</code></td><td>A producer, with its token</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Decide</td><td><code>POST /cards/&#123;id&#125;/decision</code></td><td>The person, through the head</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    <code>GET /</code> describes the head: whose it is, and which extensions it implements. The head never calls a
    producer, so a producer needs no inbound port. Giving work back to agents (orders) is an extension on the same card.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it is shaped this way</h2>
  <dl class="why">
    <dt>Identity gives idempotency</dt>
    <dd>
      The producer mints the id, so a retry re-sends the same id and gets <code>200</code>, never a duplicate.
      <a href={rfc('5')}>§5</a>
    </dd>
    <dt>One writer per card</dt>
    <dd>
      A producer owns its namespace and is the only one writing there, so there is no conflict handling.
      <a href={rfc('5')}>§5</a>, <a href={rfc('10')}>§10</a>
    </dd>
    <dt>Pull, never push</dt>
    <dd>
      Every connection starts at the producer, so an agent inside a locked network needs one egress rule.
      <a href={rfc('12')}>§12</a>
    </dd>
    <dt>A decision is a record</dt>
    <dd>
      A card is locked once decided; a change is a new card that supersedes it. <a href={rfc('6')}>§6</a>
    </dd>
    <dt>Presentation is part of the contract</dt>
    <dd>
      The lead, the proposal and the controls are specified, so every head shows a card the same way.
      <a href={rfc('3.1')}>§3.1</a>, <a href={rfc('4.5')}>§4.5</a>
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <p><a class="cta" href={href('/rfc/')}>Read the RFC, draft {RFC_FILE.version}</a></p>

  <ul class="links">
    <li><a href={href('/producers/')}>Producers</a> <span class="muted">— send a first card with curl, <code>@pbcp/client</code> or the MCP server.</span></li>
    <li><a href={href('/connectors/')}>Connectors</a> <span class="muted">— the example producers in the repository and their settings.</span></li>
    <li><a href={href('/heads/')}>Heads</a> <span class="muted">— what a head is, and the conformance suite.</span></li>
    <li><a href={href('/changelog/')}>Changelog</a> <span class="muted">— every change between drafts.</span></li>
  </ul>
</Base>

<style>
  .flow { margin: 8px 0 24px; }
  .flow svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; overflow: visible; }
  .flow .tall { display: none; max-width: 328px; margin: 0 auto; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .flow .wide { display: none; }
    .flow .tall { display: block; }
  }
  .flow .box { fill: var(--surface); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .flow .title { font: 500 19px var(--serif); fill: var(--text); text-anchor: middle; }
  .flow .sub { font: 400 12px var(--sans); fill: var(--muted); text-anchor: middle; }
  .flow .code { font: 400 11.5px var(--mono); fill: var(--muted); text-anchor: middle; }
  .flow .code.end { text-anchor: end; }
  .flow .code.start { text-anchor: start; }
  .flow .note { font: 400 12px var(--sans); fill: var(--muted); text-anchor: middle; }
  .flow .arrow { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; fill: none; }
  .flow .tip { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; }
  .why dt { font-weight: 600; margin-top: 14px; }
  .why dd { margin: 2px 0 0; }
</style>
